a0a1a673e4498ec5397aec929e4","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":15},{"dia_id":"D20:16","global_turn_index":350,"locator":"[S20T16]","raw_turn_sha256":"6b3d541af5a34c1a50cdcf1f95f3c0162e3c328941c4a665162937a690146fc0","rendered_turn_sha256":"e588104ec8b641d435d275299a50d7d1e0bf14d0e5f7f2bea48cf6e1859fb7f5","session_date":"2023-09-22","session_datetime":"2023-09-22T20:57:00","session_id":"session_20","session_index":20,"source_sha256":"88f9345d11f1566f105129a1fb2860cc7f3e15ffea46b9e366b828f7d5ab85c5","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":16},{"dia_id":"D20:17","global_turn_index":351,"locator":"[S20T17]","raw_turn_sha256":"22496ea79f87055acf3407a3cf7e01ffeef12f905126ae4e7d516a474974f356","rendered_turn_sha256":"2823b409434711bb9b9b7f01555bcda739d9c4cce99b64018dce141d64934ad6","session_date":"2023-09-22","session_datetime":"2023-09-22T20:57:00","session_id":"session_20","session_index":20,"source_sha256":"4f416335302e49aa23f892688ffdc2a5becb01468a355a42eec0f0e927e80ab0","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":17}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s3","store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- On 2023-09-22, caught up with Dave (\"Hey Calvin, good to catch up again!\"): Dave told him he'd been working on the engine of the vintage Mustang — thought he'd fixed it, but when he started it up he heard a weird noise — \"So disappointing after putting so much work in\" — and asked Calvin to look at the engine (photo of a car engine with a small engine; details in the Car mod workshop (2023-08-11) section of /memories/dave.md); Calvin sympathized — \"sorry to hear about the car trouble. That must be disappointing after putting so much work into it. Yeah, fixing cars can be tricky.\" — then shared a photo of his red sports car (Ferrari) parked in a parking lot: \"It's a sign of my hard work and dedication. Looking at it reminds me how far I've come.\" (details in ## New luxury car (Ferrari, 2023-03-26)); Dave: \"I love the way the sunlight hits this. It's definitely a great symbol of all your hard work. I bet you feel really proud when you look at it.\" and asked if there were any special memories with it; Calvin: an amazing drive \"one summer day\" — \"The wind blowing through my hair and the rush of freedom - it was unforgettable\" — and he's \"pondered the intricacies of life, taking a moment to truly appreciate the path I've chosen and the decisions that have shaped my journey\"; also said his trip to Japan was incredible — \"the culture, the people, everything was so cool\" — \"I'm already longing to go back, it was an experience that made all the hard work worth it.\" (details in ## Japan plan); Dave: \"Wow, Calvin, that's awesome! That feeling of freedom in the summer is the best. A moment of reflection not only makes the journey interesting but also productive!\" and asked whether any song from Calvin's childhood brings back memories; Calvin: \"there's this one song that always makes me smile. It played during a road trip with my dad and we had so much fun singing along to it.\"; Dave: \"Sounds awesome, Calvin! Road trips with family are always a treat. What's the name of the song?\"; Calvin: \"We used to rock a song by Tupac and Dr. Dre called 'California Love.' Ah, those were the days!\" (details in ## Music); Dave: \"Sounds great, Cal! 'California Love' is a classic! Let me know if you wanna jam some music together!\"; Calvin: \"Yeah, let's do it! That would be awesome.\" — the two are now planning to jam some music together; Dave: \"I'm stoked, Calvin! We can crank up the music and have an awesome jam session. Can't wait!\"; Calvin: \"Yeah, Dave! Gonna be great! Can't wait to see what we can do.\"; Dave: \"Yeah, let's do it! It'll be awesome. Let's rock it!\"; Calvin: \"Yeah, let's do this! I can't wait!\"; the conversation closed with Dave: \"Nice one, Calvin! Let's make some awesome memories and have a great time. See ya soon!\", and Calvin: \"Count me in. Can't wait to create something special. See you soon!\", and Dave's final parting: \"Yep, Calvin! Can't wait to see you soon. Take it easy till then.\" [S20T1][S20T2][S20T3][S20T4][S20T5][S20T6][S20T7][S20T8][S20T9][S20T10][S20T11][S20T12][S20T13][S20T14][S20T15][S20T16][S20T17].","text_sha256":"c9171473e1d7e2e6866f3eb34d5f7ef58558a570e6115ddc8f5b6946ac3a56ed","timestamp":"2023-09-22T20:57:00"},{"attribution_index_sha256":"98109144a5a23da7a5b89634be2c543ea2366f2abe85f1f3f8a3df64a5e92ce2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D20:1","D20:2","D20:3","D20:4","D20:5","D20:6","D20:7","D20:8","D20:9","D20:10","D20:11","D20:12","D20:13","D20:14","D20:15","D20:16","D20:17"],"kind":"curated_fact","line_end":212,"line_start":212,"source_locators":["[S20T1]","[S20T2]","[S20T3]","[S20T4]","[S20T5]","[S20T6]","[S20T7]","[S20T8]","[S20T9]","[S20T10]","[S20T11]","[S20T12]","[S20T13]","[S20T14]","[S20T15]","[S20T16]","[S20T17]"],"text_sha256":"6296e7905e8d71be742841987b19e24f6c77d1c25a24a17f47105e5fc74a6d7e"}],"dia_ids":["D20:1","D20:2","D20:3","D20:4","D20:5","D20:6","D20:7","D20:8","D20:9","D20:10","D20:11","D20:12","D20:13","D20:14","D20:15","D20:16","D20:17"],"evidence_id":"ev-d062a89d3a637af772db99a2602b362ac1da11e00b0edbee5f2639385810bf1d","group_id":"/memories/dave.md > # Dave","line_end":212,"line_start":212,"observation_ids":["obs-0003"],"path":"/memories/dave.md","query_terms":[],"rank":null,"records_sha256":"130a5a1e1b75083358ef27a98dd215a4e75c819ace6f2ee9b560ba394e0f0394","retrieval_round":4,"schema_version":1,"score":null,"section":"# Dave > ## Relationships","selection_ordinal":3,"session_id":"session_20","source_kind":"curated","source_locators":["[S20T1]","[S20T2]","[S20T3]","[S20T4]","[S20T5]","[S20T6]","[S20T7]","[S20T8]","[S20T9]","[S20T10]","[S20T11]","[S20T12]","[S20T13]","[S20T14]","[S20T15]","[S20T16]","[S20T17]"],"source_map_sha256":"6e99115961bae06a48bfb7e82dbdcc18dc32ccf6c5ce57e3c266dfc7a5d4d574","source_records":[{"dia_id":"D20:1","global_turn_index":335,"locator":"[S20T1]","raw_turn_sha256":"c7bf